<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bareilly</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bareilly is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Ramganga River, and the main city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilkhand">Rohilkhand</a> region. It became the seat of the Rohilla chiefs under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafiz-rahmat-khan">Hafiz Rahmat Khan</a> in the mid-18th century. After passing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> in 1774, it was ceded to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1801 and was a centre of the revolt of 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bareilly.jpg" alt="Bareilly" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wp masifnoor · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dargah_Aala_Hazrat_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
